   "type": "h2",
   "text": "5.4 Data sources and gaps"
  },
  {
   "type": "lead",
   "text": "Arrivals, seats and cruise volumes can be tracked from existing feeds; spread, bookability, jobs and community spend cannot until new data is built or shared."
  },
  {
   "type": "p",
   "text": "Stakeholders put data among the top barriers: no approved methodology exists for provincial tourism GDP and jobs (Stakeholder Insights Report, Mar 2026, p37), and no one holds a single view of visitor behaviour (Current State Diagnostic, Dec 2025, p56, p57). The data-sharing protocol under focus area 18 (I16) is the route to closing the gaps below."
  },
